# 12 -- exhaustive grid sweep (TADAH:GRID).
#
# Evaluates every point on a Cartesian grid. `STEP` is the number of
# samples per dimension (total cost = STEP ^ dim), so keep dim and
# STEP small. Useful as a deterministic sanity-check, or to visualise
# the loss surface before reaching for a smarter optimiser.

OPTIMIZER
  STRATEGY
    TYPE PLAIN
    LIB TADAH
    ALGO GRID
    STEP 10
  ENDSTRATEGY
ENDOPTIMIZER

LOSS L2
FAILSCORE 1e16
PC_ERMSE 0 0.0001
PC_LAMMPS --script ../common/lammps/Ecoh.in --hotvar hot_a0 2.5 4.5 3.302 --varloss Ecoh 8.10 800

OPTIM RCUT2B  (1) 4.0 6.0
OPTIM SGRIDMB (1) 0.1 0.4

OUTPUT 1
BOUTPUT 1
